KNOWNBUG gcc16
main.cpp
--cpp11 --unwind 2 --no-unwinding-assertions --no-built-in-assertions
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
GCC 16's std::list uses __allocated_obj with a move constructor
from __allocated_ptr. The brace-init unwrapping works but the
constructor call has a type mismatch: the argument is a value
type but the parameter expects an rvalue reference. This is a
separate bug in rvalue reference parameter handling for
constructor calls generated by implicit conversion.
